TOPIC OF FREE-CONTENT IS BUSINESS RELATED CONTENT ONLY

This list is well publicized, but often new members are unaware
that the topic of this list is "SMALL BUSINESS RELATED ARTICLES"
and it is an article distribution list, not an announcement list.
Issues that address matters of concern to small business online
such as marketing, promotion, search engines, staff or personal
development, site design, time management, incorporation, taxes
software (no geek speak), partnerships, start-ups, joint venture
resources and other small business topics will be considered.

We've expanded topics slightly to include finance, real estate
and investment articles, but will scrutinize those submissions
more thoroughly for link spamming abuses described above due to
the prevalence of finance, investment and loan related splogs
and auto-generated sites of any kind intended solely to display
Google Adsense or Yahoo Publisher Network ads.


LINKING RESTRICTIONS

Articles including self promotional links in the article body or
promotions of affiliate programs will be deleted. If the link to
affiliate programs is included in your signature or resource box
it may be included but links are limited to three. NO promotional
text, autoresponder addresses or self referencing links within
articles will be allowed. No new website announcements or 
ebook offers. No more than three links of any kind allowed in
resource boxes. You cannot own domains referenced within article.

It has become necessary to restrict and limit links due to
search engine spamming abuses emerging in article marketing.

Article Dashboard sites in linked articles not accepted.
Plug In Profit sites in linked articles not accepted.

We reserve the right to delete articles based on redirects or
splog URL's used in author resource boxes. URL's that auto-
matically redirect to secondary sites not allowed. Links are
checked in Whois records for ownership by authors and domains
linked from resource boxes will be limited to three sites owned
or controlled by the author. If those domains are reserved with
proxy registrars or information is hidden in Whois records, the
articles will be deleted. Writers or marketers distributing an
article on behalf of clients must state in usage restrictions
or the resource box that the linked sites belong to clients.

POLICIES, SUMMARIES, RESTRICTIONS AND FORMATTING

Articles full of bizarre characters that result from writers
cutting and pasting directly from word processor
software into an email to submit to the list. Plain ascii
text cannot reproduce much of the punctuation from WP
software so you must first paste it into Notepad and remove
those characters first before submitting to the list. 

Further Reading on this can be found at the following URL:

http://shorl.com/benystulogrubri  (redirects to article)

Articles which use any phrase repeatedly in an attempt to gain
rank for that phrase will be deleted without comment. A rule of
thumb would be no more than one use of any keyword phrase
per 100 words. If your article is 600 words long and you've
parroted a keyword phrase more than six times - that is too
many uses of the same phrase. (And it's poor writing)

Duplicate articles are expressly forbidden and this should
serve as notice that if that is detected, you will be banned 
from the list when duplicates are detected. Changing titles to 
submit duplicates is not acceptable. Duplicates are detected  
by content management software upon distribution to our new
site at http://Publish101.com and will result in your removal 
from the list.

Please remember to include a short summary of your article, along
with a word count and resource box to facilitate publishers
contacting you directly through web site links and e-mail links.
Mention any publication restrictions and requests for copies of
publications that your articles appear in. 

One of the most critical issues for list members is FORMATTING!
A free resource allowing cut and paste or file upload is at:
http://www.formatit.com Please use that source to format because
when you cut and paste from many word processing programs, the
"hard return" is not saved and formatting is lost. Always use
a hard return at the end of each line, with lines no longer than
64 characters. If your posts are not formatted in this manner,
your articles will be deleted. No publishers will spend the time
to format your work for you.

Email readers wrap text at 64 characters. IF you lines are 
longer than 64 characters without a hard return - you'll get 
alternating long and short lines to your text. It's very hard 
to read and will stop most editors from using your work.

Finally, a resource box linking to your website is the best
value you get from distributed articles. Make certain that
your URL is complete in the resource box so that automated
content management systems can hyperlink it so you get
"credit" for your work. A complete URL will not be created
unless you include the http:// ahead of www.domain.com
So the proper URL is http://www.domain.com 

Also don't include periods or punctuation after a domain as
it will cause an error when linking to your site in most cases.

Please resubmit once notified of rejection of articles to:

mailto:free-content@yahoogroups.com

